      },
      "description": "Metrics: gtfs_rt_vehicle_computed_speed, gtfs_rt_vehicle_speed_discrepancy_ratio, gtfs_rt_vehicle_speed_last_computed_timestamp_seconds\nQuestion answered: \"Are vehicles reporting unrealistic speeds, and how old is each retained calculation?\"\n\nVisualization: Histogram\nRationale: A histogram buckets computed speeds into ranges, making it trivial to spot an anomalous right-tail (speeds > 100 km/h for a city bus). This is far more effective than a time series for isolating the fraction of vehicles reporting physically impossible speeds.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 45
      },
      "id": 501,
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "gtfs_rt_vehicle_computed_speed{agency_id=~\"$agency_id\",server_url=~\"$server_url\"}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "name": "Prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "gtfs_rt_vehicle_speed_discrepancy_ratio{agency_id=~\"$agency_id\",server_url=~\"$server_url\"}",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "name": "Prometheus"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "time() - gtfs_rt_vehicle_speed_last_computed_timestamp_seconds{agency_id=~\"$agency_id\",server_url=~\"$server_url\"}",
          "legendFormat": "Speed age {{vehicle_id}}",
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "name": "Prometheus"
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": "5.1 Speed Validation",
      "type": "histogram",
      "options": {
        "bucketSize": 10,
        "combine": false
      }
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
